  "evidence": "TEXT_D: Extra £2bn/year for education funded by +1p on the basic rate; early‑years provision for all 3–4s; class size caps; lifelong learning. NHS +£540m/year; recruit frontline staff; maximum six‑month waits; free eye/dental checks; new Carer’s Benefit; stronger patient rights. Robust equality agenda (women, disabled, minorities, LGBT), equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, tackle hate crime. Raise personal allowance; 50% rate over £100k; simpler Low Income Benefit; anti‑fraud/evasion. Independent Bank of England; borrow only to invest; stronger competition law; employee participation/profit‑sharing. PR, Bill of Rights, Freedom of Information; stronger local/devolved power. 30% CO2 cut; major public transport push; insulate 2m low‑income homes; tax shift from jobs to pollution.\n\nTEXT_C: Independence negotiations and referendum; Scottish Defence Forces; remove Trident; phased withdrawal from NATO. Social measures: higher child benefit; restore 16–17 benefits; pensioner top‑ups and end means‑testing for residential care; NHS +£35m/year; ban tobacco advertising; affordable housing build; free nursery education; hire 700 teachers; restore student grants. Economy/tax: business tax cuts; 15p starter rate; widen basic band; remove NI ceiling for higher earners; cut VAT on fuel; introduce minimum wage; charter for trade union rights. Governance: written constitution with social rights; PR; abolish unelected influence; vote at 16; public petitions. Environment/land: invest in renewables; phase out nuclear; double woodland; land reform.",
